        "text": "Team, please refactor the Customer Ledger page (`/admin/customer-ledger` or `CustomerLedgerDirectory.tsx`):\n\n1. Clean Up Top KPI Summary Cards:\n- Delete the 2 middle cards:\n  - Remove \"B2C RETAIL\" card (7 Retail accounts).\n  - Remove \"B2B CORPORATE\" card (0 Business & institutional accounts).\n- Keep only:\n  - Card 1: \"TOTAL CUSTOMERS\" (or \"TOTAL B2C CLIENTS\")\n  - Card 2: \"OUTSTANDING BALANCE\" (₹0.00 Net customer wallet liability)\n- Adjust the grid layout so the remaining 2 cards fit cleanly (e.g., `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4`).\n\n2. Remove Customer Type Filter & Toggle:\n- In the search and filter toolbar:\n  - Completely remove the \"CUSTOMER TYPE\" filter toggle button group (`All (7)`, `B2C (7)`, `B2B (0)`).\n  - Retain the customer search input (`Filter by customer name, email, phone, or UUID...`) and the `Rows per page` dropdown.\n\n3. Enforce Strict B2C Query Filtering:\n- Update the fetch query to strictly filter and fetch ONLY B2C customers:\n  - Apply condition: `.eq('customer_type', 'B2C')` (or `customer_type IS NULL OR customer_type = 'B2C'`).\n  - Completely exclude any B2B corporate profiles or accounts from this ledger directory.\n\n4. Table Column Refinement:\n- In the table body, the \"TYPE\" column currently shows `B2C Retail` badge for all rows. Either simplify it or remove the redundant `TYPE` column completely since this entire page is exclusively for B2C Retail Customers.\n\nPlease apply these layout and query updates now to streamline the Customer Ledger.",
